<h2 id="continue-building">5. Continue building</h2>

<p>
  Tell Copilot what you want to change. If the badge shows an error, give Copilot
  the error message as best as you can and ask it to try to fix it.
  If anything is unclear, ask a volunteer for help.
</p>

<p>
  Reconnect the badge if needed. The skill handles Disk Mode for the next copy;
  follow Copilot's steps to copy and test the updated app.
</p>

<p>
  When updating your own app, tell Copilot it is an update so it uses the skill's
  replacement option and keeps a backup. Do not replace someone else's app or
  change shared badge files.
</p>

<p>
  If Copilot cannot copy your app, ask it for the full path to your checked app
  folder and the correct BADGER destination. With Copilot's guidance, you can
  copy that one folder in File Explorer on Windows or Finder on macOS, then
  eject and test as above. Do not disable broad safety settings to give access.
</p>
